<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Junkers</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Junkers was a German aircraft and engine manufacturer based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a>, founded by the engineer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hugo-junkers">Hugo Junkers</a>. It built early all-metal aircraft and the Ju 52 transport, and after its takeover by the Nazi state in 1935 produced warplanes such as the Ju 87 Stuka and Ju 88 bomber. After 1945 its works in Dessau were dismantled by the Soviet occupiers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/junkers.jpg" alt="Junkers" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-R14718,_Dessau,_Junkers-Werke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>East of the Elbe, <b>Junker</b> landlords held estates worked by dependent peasants under the manorial system known as Gutsherrschaft, and the nobility supplied the officer corps, while townspeople paid the excise.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>From the fifteenth century the nobility, the <b>Junkers</b>, turned their estates into large grain-producing manors worked by peasants bound by heavy labour services, a system of manorial lordship, Gutsherrschaft, that shaped east-Elbian society until the nineteenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/margraviate-of-brandenburg">Margraviate of Brandenburg · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Hugo Junkers founded his first works at Dessau in 1895, later the base of the <b>Junkers</b> aircraft factory.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-anhalt">Duchy of Anhalt</a></li><li><blockquote>Its industries included the <b>Junkers</b> aircraft works and chemical plants at Bitterfeld nearby.</blockquote><a href="/state/free-state-of-anhalt">Free State of Anhalt</a></li></ul></section>
